      "keep_going_semantics": "Stop at action exhaustion or failure unless keep_going; aggregate ok is sticky.",
      "selection": "Match is already selected; NL scoring and ambiguity resolution remain native.",
      "child_iteration": "Generator carries domain_index, name_index, current names and entries through the finite DOMAIN_CATALOG; each domain must have 20 names, then the complete list is checked and sliced to default limit 500.",
      "index_iteration": "Indexer carries file cursor, insertion results and index/search outputs; this invocation has one input file, Bloom/embedding/search enabled and Vampire disabled.",
      "termination": "Catalog and file exhaustion return normally; there is no scientific search, retry, feedback or theorem promotion loop."
    },
    "mathformer.operation_notes": {
      "initialize": "Initialize the native ordered route accumulator.",
      "select": "Select the native action at len(state.children), restoring source-owned route metadata and scoring evidence.",
      "dispatch": "scripts/mathformer.py:run_action -> run_leaf_action owns admission, preflight, dry-run handling, subprocess launch/capture and write audit. Resolve the source-owned registry and repository mount; this action has no dependencies and no extra arguments. Admission rejection or preflight errors return failure data. Dry-run returns without launching. Otherwise launch tests/kb/run_famous_theorem_corpus.py --json. Its main orders prepare -> generate_read -> index -> probe -> assess -> emit. prepare resets artifacts/kb/famous_corpus_test; generate_read runs the generator then parses nonblank JSONL records. index ingests that one file, builds Bloom filters, builds 256-dimensional embeddings, then searches Fundamental theorem of algebra with k=5; Vampire ingestion is disabled. probe uses the same KB and index hits for name/any exact membership, an absent name, and target-versus-unrelated geometric distances. assess consumes paths, generated report/records, index report and probes: check 500 entries, unique IDs, generated_candidate status, informal hashes, insertion counts, index files, target retrieval and distance evidence. emit prints the payload and returns 0 iff all assertions pass, otherwise 3. Generator/indexer nonzero exits raise immediately; parsing, I/O and KB exceptions abort the child process. The hub captures nonzero child exits as ok=false; a failed write audit also forces ok=false and status=undeclared_writes even after returncode=0. Unexpected launch exceptions propagate.",
      "advance": "Append the child once and stop at action exhaustion or native failure policy; action_count is one.",
      "finish": "Complete the native route with source-owned metadata, sticky aggregate ok and ordered child observations."
    }
